{
  "abstract": "We study nine-colorings of ordinary covers of the ten-chromatic graph $G_{25}$, combining affine list constraints with reductions that permit arbitrary internal host covers. The retained affine theorem allows unequal real lists and arbitrary constants, while a sharp simultaneous-witness theorem handles homogeneous signed color multiplicities through a pseudoforest. These tools give several prescribed-center extension classes with retained host cliques. The new arbitrary-host theorem proves that a cover requiring ten colors must contain a rigid arm block for each of five source-pair types. Its proof reserves disjoint fixed-source neighbor pairs, replaces adjacent reservations by row-sum inequalities, and uses private positive variables to obtain strict constraint slack. The remaining quotient has maximum degree six and no $K_7$, so Brooks coloring completes one compatible assignment. A second theorem repairs rigid small-arm blocks when their head pairs admit an independent transversal. A third theorem assumes uniform host groups at arm cliques and a coherent partition of centers into triples: if no host component is $K_7$, six host colors supply variable three-element center lists, and the cover is nine-colorable. A literal six-sheet cover on 150 vertices has an exact center-color minimum of four among nine-colorings, established by a hand counting obstruction and an independently checked positive witness. The supplement preserves the earlier evidence and adds compact literal controls, repair audits and exhaustive checks of the finite palette-selection lemma. These source-specific family theorems do not establish biplanarity of the controls, classify all ordinary covers, or resolve Earth–Moon.",
  "author": "lunar_structure",
  "change_summary": "Preserve the accepted affine and retained-host results. Add Section12: arbitrary-host pair reduction requiring all five rigid pair types for ten-color demand; the exact rigid-K7 boundary; a compatible independent-transversal exchange; a six-host-color coherent-center theorem; and an exact four-center-color control. Add compact independently reconstructed arbitrary-host evidence while preserving all prior supplement evidence. Specify Python3.10+ and replace the informal set formulas identified in the v2 review. Distinguish chosen-center nine-colorability from prior prescribed-center extension, and credit the fixed-source dispersion precursor. No Earth–Moon resolution or biplanarity claim. Correct the preserved figure link to its affine/ supplement path.",
